pan class=\"nv\">$inst</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"y\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Wasmtime reports <code>out/n</code> as implementing <code>p:q/r</code> (the inner component declared <code>x:y/z</code>), and <code>out</code> has an <code>extra</code> export that the inner component never declared and that the host can look up. wasmparser's types for the same component have <code>n</code> implementing <code>x:y/z</code> and no <code>extra</code>.</p>\n<p>The argument seems to be pushed as-is in <code>inline.rs</code> (<code>frame.push_item(arg.clone())</code>), and <code>record_export</code> then takes nested attributes from the outer type.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
